nderlies autoinflammatory disorders. Through a cytometry-based screen, Coombs               et al.               showed that whereas the NLRP3 and NLRP6 members of the NOD-like receptor family formed inflammasomes in cells, NLRP12 did not. Rather, NLRP12 acted as an endogenous inhibitor of NLRP3 inflammasome formation. A mutant form of NLRP12 implicated in autoinflammatory disease failed to suppress NLRP3 inflammasome activation, suggesting that NLRP3 inhibitors currently in clinical trials should be considered to treat NLRP12-associated autoinflammatory disorders. —John F. Foley},
